1
00:00:04,629 --> 00:00:06,629
[GROANS]

2
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:14,427
[CONTINUES GROANING]

3
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:18,309
(Leonard:)Problem?

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,520
- This is Thai food.
- Here we go.

5
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:25,067
(Sheldon:)We don't have Thai food on Thursday.
We have pizza on Thursday.

6
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:27,943
(Leonard:)Yes, but we all agreed
the third Thursday of every month...

7
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,111
(Leonard:)...would be
Anything Can Happen Thursday.

8
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,450
(Sheldon:)The news didn't reach
my digestive system which, when startled...

9
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:36,786
(Sheldon:)...has its own version
of Anything Can Happen Thursday.

10
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:40,708
(Howard:)The whole idea behind
Anything Can Happen Thursday...

11
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,834
(Howard:)...is to get out of this rut
we've been in.

12
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:45,631
(Sheldon:)Rut? I think you mean consistency.

13
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:48,675
(Sheldon:)And if we're going to abandon that,
why even call it Thursday?

14
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:53,340
Let's call it "Quonko Day" and divide it
into 29 hours of 17 minutes a piece...

15
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:57,181
(Sheldon:)...and celebrate it by sacrificing a goat
to the mighty god Ra.

16
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:02,022
(Raj:)I could go for some goat.

